## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical, measurable diagnostics for cross-region latency without code changes, focusing on network-layer factors and real-world tooling. It emphasizes data collection, hypothesis-driven testing, and concrete mitigations across DNS, CDN, and edge routing.

## Key Concepts
- Anycast and IXP ECMP behavior under load
- DNS latency vs HTTP latency as diagnostic signals
- TLS SNI routing at CDNs and edge caches
- CDN origin fetch queuing and caching strategies

